<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Edward Augustus Freeman</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1823">1823</a>–<a href="/years/1892">1892</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Edward Augustus Freeman was an English historian and Regius Professor of Modern History at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oxford">Oxford</a> from 1884. His best-known work is the History of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norman-conquest">Norman Conquest</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, and in his History of Federal Government he made the Achaean League a model of a federal state. Admired for his learning, he is now also criticised for his racial views of the English past.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/edward-augustus-freeman.jpg" alt="Edward Augustus Freeman" width="320" height="436" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Elliott &amp; Fry · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Edward_Augustus_Freeman.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
